       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged vasodilatory shock. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nCould this be a typo? Here are some common ones:\n- **10 mg once daily** is the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg once daily** is the typical starting dose, and 2.5 mg is used for frail patients.\n- **3 mg** may have been intended if this was a different drug or a slip.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. If you'd like a corrected dose, give me the number and I'll enter it right away."
      }
